<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24068" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-sŭpĕrābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>that cannot be passed over.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>insurmountable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transitus Alpium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					21, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">via,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 36</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Unconquerable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus bello,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 4, 40</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput bello,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 613</span></i>
			.— Of a disease, <i>incurable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">valetudo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 2, 2</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Unavoidable</i>, <i>inevitable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 15, 807</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">necessitas fati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					13, 1</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insŭpĕrābĭ-lĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>unconquerably</i>, Aug. Civ. Dei, 5, 8.</div>
